{"timestamp": "2026-02-04 18:04:06.728988", "event": "llm_start", "messages": "content=\"You are provided with the following network description and its current state:\\nNetwork Description: A 4-tier data center Clos (super-spine, spine, leaf, service hosts) using EBGP: all inter-router links are /31s from 172.16.0.0/16, and each leaf connects to one service subnet 10.<pod>.<idx>.0/24 that it advertises via BGP.Each pod runs one DNS server (Bind, authoritative for zone podX) and several HTTP web servers; DNS provides A records like web0.pod0 pointing to the web servers, which run python3 -m http.server on port 80.External client hosts sit in 192.168.<pod>.0/24 networks, use the pod DNS servers in /etc/resolv.conf, and access the services via URLs such as http://web0.pod0 over the routed Clos fabric.\\nHosts: client_0, client_1\\nDns Servers: dns_pod0, dns_pod1\\nWeb Servers: webserver0_pod0, webserver0_pod1, webserver1_pod0, webserver1_pod1, webserver2_pod0, webserver2_pod1\\nRouters (FRRRouting): leaf_router_0_0, leaf_router_0_1, leaf_router_0_2, leaf_router_0_3, leaf_router_1_0, leaf_router_1_1, leaf_router_1_2, leaf_router_1_3, spine_router_0_0, spine_router_0_1, spine_router_0_2, spine_router_0_3, spine_router_1_0, spine_router_1_1, spine_router_1_2, spine_router_1_3, super_spine_router_0, super_spine_router_1\\nTopology: (leaf_router_0_0:eth4, dns_pod0:eth0), (leaf_router_0_1:eth4, webserver0_pod0:eth0), (leaf_router_0_2:eth4, webserver1_pod0:eth0), (leaf_router_0_3:eth4, webserver2_pod0:eth0), (leaf_router_1_0:eth4, dns_pod1:eth0), (leaf_router_1_1:eth4, webserver0_pod1:eth0), (leaf_router_1_2:eth4, webserver1_pod1:eth0), (leaf_router_1_3:eth4, webserver2_pod1:eth0), (spine_router_0_0:eth2, leaf_router_0_0:eth0), (spine_router_0_0:eth3, leaf_router_0_1:eth0), (spine_router_0_0:eth4, leaf_router_0_2:eth0), (spine_router_0_0:eth5, leaf_router_0_3:eth0), (spine_router_0_1:eth2, leaf_router_0_0:eth1), (spine_router_0_1:eth3, leaf_router_0_1:eth1), (spine_router_0_